-Sources, and the rule for combining them (the same rule chapter 10 states for its table):
-
-* before: benchmarks/results/main/summary.csv, the retained bundle measured at commit 3c91662
-  with each process pinned to one CPU (rows with series "ExecFloat binary proved software");
-* after: pass5-final-summary.csv (2026-09-07, widths 4 to 4096, unpinned), overridden where
-  both runs measured a width by pass5-final2-summary.csv (same day, later working tree with the
-  two-limb code generation fixes). Only widths with both a before and an after row are drawn,
-  so the custom 24, 48, 96 and 112 bit layouts of pass5-final2 are not plotted.
-
-The speed-up labels at 16 and 32 bits are before/after rounded to two significant figures,
-which is how chapter 10 rounds every speed-up, so the plot and the table always agree.
-Every string drawn on the figure is checked for em and en dashes before saving, because the
-site's text checks cannot see inside a PNG.
-
-Run from anywhere: python3 plot_pass5_before_after.py [--out PNG]
