-Three changes account for most of this, and each is visible in the kernel the planner now selects. First, one-word IEEE formats up to 64 bits gained an addition and subtraction kernel that stays entirely in `UInt64`: field decoding, alignment, signed-magnitude combination, and rounding without a single `Nat` allocation. Its capacity contract is [[LeanFloat.Floats.Formats.BinaryInterchange.Model.NativeSmallWordAdd.Eligible]]: an IEEE layout of at most 64 bits with at most 30 exponent bits and at most 61 fraction bits, which covers every standard one-word IEEE format, binary64 included. A one-word layout with a wider exponent field, which `FloatFormat.ieee` allows, falls back to the storage decoder and the shared exact kernel.
+## One API, several kernels
 
-Second, the dispatchers ([[LeanFloat.Floats.Formats.BinaryInterchange.Model.AddBackend.word]] and its siblings, proved equal to the specification by [[LeanFloat.Floats.Formats.BinaryInterchange.Model.AddBackend.word_eq_spec]]) are specialized to the descriptor ([chapter 06](#/chapter/the-numerical-models)), and each eligibility test is written as a plain conditional on the descriptor's fields rather than as a typeclass instance the compiler cannot see through, so for a fixed format the compiler evaluates the test once and keeps only the branch that applies.
+The FloatLean curve is one public API, not one algorithm. The planner changes implementation as
+the format changes:
 
-Third, the configured instances make the dispatcher itself the public entry point whenever [[LeanFloat.Floats.Formats.BinaryInterchange.Configured.StoragePlan.firstOrderDispatch]] holds, which is the case for the machine-word plans and for wide plans that satisfy [[LeanFloat.Floats.Formats.BinaryInterchange.Model.NativePair.Eligible]]. A monomorphic `x + y` then compiles to one call into a copy of the dispatcher with the layout constants folded in, instead of first fetching the planner's stored choice, a closure that carries its proof, and then calling it on operands the runtime has had to box. None of this cost us trust. The dispatcher that now serves as the entry point is proved equal to the specification, the public operation is proved equal to the same specification ([[LeanFloat.Floats.ExecFloat.Capability.run_eq_spec]]), and the choice `#float_info` reports is proved to be the choice the certified selector makes ([[LeanFloat.Floats.ExecFloat.Backend.selectCertified_estimate]]), so the speed came from removing indirection, not from stepping outside the proved path.
+- very small formats may use exhaustive tables;
+- one-word layouts use native-word kernels;
+- binary32 and binary64 have monomorphic fixed-format routes;
+- eligible formats up to 128 bits use fixed-limb kernels; and
+- wider or unsupported operation/format combinations use the exact general engine.
 
